    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70520" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νευρ-όω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>strain the sinews, nerve,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάθος καὶ τοὺς ἀσθενεστάτους ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.48
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῶμα νεότητι καὶ ἀκμῇ νευρούμενον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					3.49
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be supplied with nerves, innervated,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρά</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				8.236
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ . . , ἐκ</span> . . , <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>UP</u>
				9.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				16.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νενεύρωται,</span> sens. obsc. (cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεῦρον</span> v), but metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. ἥδε ξυμφορά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					1078
				</span></i>
			.</div>
